# Theme system (mandatory)

Every new UI component and page must be theme-aware by default and must use the centralized global theme system. Never implement an independent theme mechanism.

## Required

- Use semantic tokens from `src/app/globals.css` (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-card`, etc.).
- Use `ThemeProvider` only from `src/components/theme/theme-provider.tsx` (already mounted in the root layout).
- Use `useTheme` from `@/hooks/use-theme` for client theme reads/writes.
- Use `ThemeToggle` from `@/components/theme/theme-toggle` for UI controls.
- Support Light, Dark, and System via the existing `next-themes` integration.

## Forbidden

- Per-page or per-component theme state
- Extra theme providers
- Scattered `localStorage` theme access
- Hardcoded theme-specific colors for general UI chrome (`bg-floral-white`, `text-smoky-black`, raw hex) without a documented exception
- Converting entire layouts/pages to Client Components just for theming

## Reference

See `docs/design-system/THEMING.md` for architecture, tokens, and testing.
